        "original_id": "fe7bda70-e4aa-51b5-af6b-a1fad36ffd2f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ike Turner, Tina Turner\n- Organizations: Kings of Rhythm, Ike & Tina Turner Revue\n- Places: Clarksdale, Mississippi\n- Topics: Rhythm and blues, soul, rock and roll\n\nFacts:\n- The Kings of Rhythm are an American rhythm and blues and soul group that formed in the late 1940s in Clarksdale, Mississippi.\n- Ike Turner led the Kings of Rhythm from their formation until his death in 2007.\n- Ike Turner was an early pioneer of 1950s rock and roll.\n- Ike Turner is most popularly known for his work with Tina Turner in the Ike & Tina Turner Revue during the 1960s and 1970s.",
